-- examples/checks/asks-hole.rofl — hole ASKED IS EVERY RULE'S HOLES (the conservative reading, decided 2026-10-05).
-- ho_ok and hole are asked. A cone would list only the holes of the rules that ran, and ho_bad's division by zero is
-- in no premise of ho_ok's: asked, hole is a question about every rule, so every rule is kept (said in the
-- diagnostics) and ho_bad's hole is the whole world's. The holes of the rules a cone runs are in the store whether
-- or not hole is asked.
asks(ho_ok).
asks(hole).
edb(ho_src).
ho_src(1). ho_src(0).
ho_ok(X) :- ho_src(X).
ho_bad(Y) :- ho_src(X), Y is 10 / X.
-- expect-row: ho_bad[main](10)
-- expect-row: hole[$kernel]($rule(
